Searching in Arrays 
Searching in an array means finding whether a particular value exists in the array and, if it exists, finding its position (index).

Example:
Array:  [10, 25, 30, 45, 50]
Index:   0   1   2   3   4

Search: 30
Answer: index 2


Two main searching techniques
 1. Linear Search
 2. Binary Search

Linear search checks the elements one by one from the beginning until it finds the target.

Example:


Array = [10, 25, 30, 45, 50]
Target = 45


Binary Search:

Binary search is much faster, but there is an important condition:

The array must be sorted.

Example:

Array = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70]
Target = 60

Instead of checking every element, binary search repeatedly checks the middle.

[10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70]
               ↑
             middle

10 → 25 → 30 → 45 
                 ↑
              Found!




